# Email style — short, human

- **Open with the substance.** No "thank you for…", "just wanted to…", "I hope this finds you well".
- **Body length:** acknowledgement / bug-fix < 200 words. Kickoff 4–8 short paragraphs.
- **One card.** No stacked gradient + callouts + sectioned headings in the same email.
- **One quote, one link, one ask.** Don't restate.
- **No hedging** ("we think", "hopefully"), no emoji, no flourish dashes.
- **Numbers stay numbers** (score, count, time). Don't paraphrase them.
- **The plain-text version is the canary.** If it sounds bloated in text, the HTML is bloated.

Recipient is a 13-year-old or his parent. Talk to them, not at them.
